---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getRelease, site, repository } from "../lib/release";
const r = await getRelease();
const scenes = [
  [
    "01",
    "PROFILE",
    "Every profile.\nOne deliberate choice.",
    "Keep your configured accounts together. Choose the one you want, with no automatic rotation or preference for Pro. Reserved profiles and Friend Priority remain your decision.",
  ],
  [
    "02",
    "USAGE",
    "Read the limit.\nThen make your move.",
    "See remaining allowance, reset times and when the data was last confirmed. Each profile refreshes independently. Pro is allowed to have different windows from Plus.",
  ],
  [
    "03",
    "LAUNCH",
    "Your workspace.\nThe profile you choose.",
    "VeyDock prepares a shared-workspace handoff after Codex quits normally. Save your work first. Real A/B/A switching acceptance is still pending in the public alpha.",
  ],
  [
    "04",
    "QUICK",
    "Less reaching.\nMore doing.",
    "The desktop quick launcher puts profiles and actions behind Ctrl + K. Try the website demonstration here. It does not open or control your local Codex app.",
  ],
];
const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
      name: "VeyDock",
      description:
        "Windows Codex profile switcher and usage manager. Public alpha with account-switch verification pending.",
      operatingSystem: "Windows",
      applicationCategory: "DeveloperApplication",
      url: site,
      downloadUrl: r.url,
      softwareVersion: r.version,
      author: {
        "@type": "Person",
        name: "Mithil Katkoria",
        url: "https://github.com/mithilkatkoria",
      },
      offers: { "@type": "Offer", price: "0", priceCurrency: "USD" },
    },
    { "@type": "WebSite", name: "VeyDock", url: site },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="VeyDock | Codex Account Switcher for Windows"
  description="A Windows Codex profile manager for usage limits, reset times and deliberate account switching. Explore the open-source alpha, documentation and real downloads."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        VEYDOCK <span>WINDOWS UTILITY / 01</span>
      </p>
      <h1>
        Switch Codex
        <br />
        profiles.
        <br />
        <span>Keep your flow.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-description">
        A Windows Codex profile switcher and usage manager. Your accounts, usage
        windows and next move, in one control panel.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href="/download">
          Download for Windows <span>↓</span>
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href={repository}>
          Inspect the source ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="mono release-line">v{r.version} / X64 / MIT / PUBLIC ALPHA</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-media">
      <div class="media-label mono">
        <span>01 / THE CONTROL PANEL</span>
        <span>DEVELOPMENT PREVIEW</span>
      </div>
      <img
        src="/media/veydock-codex-switcher-windows.webp"
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
        alt="VeyDock profile cards displaying safe sample usage, reserved status and Open Codex controls"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <figcaption>
        Real interface. Simulated data. Newer than the current download.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="hero-bottom mono">
      <span>CHOOSE. CHECK. DOCK.</span>
      <a href="#sequence">EXPLORE THE INSTRUMENT ↓</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="editorial">
    <div class="wrap editorial-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">A SMALL TOOL FOR A SPECIFIC JOB</p>
      <h2>
        Four accounts.
        <br />
        Three accounts.
        <br />
        <span>Your accounts.</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <p>You shouldn’t have to guess which profile has room to work.</p>
        <p>
          VeyDock brings configured profiles and real Codex rate-limit readings
          into one place. No fixed account cap. No silent switching. No made-up
          production allowances.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works">
          Understand the handoff ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="sequence" class="sequence wrap">
    <div class="sequence-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE DOCKING SEQUENCE</p>
      <p class="mono">01 → 04 / UNDER YOUR CONTROL</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sequence-grid">
      <div class="rail" aria-label="Product sequence">
        {scenes.map(([n, label]) => (
          <a href={`#scene-${n}`} data-rail={n}>
            <span class="rail-dot"></span>
            <span>
              {n} / {label}
            </span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="scene-copy">
        {scenes.map(([n, label, title, body]) => (
          <section class="scene" id={`scene-${n}`} data-scene={n}>
            <p class="eyebrow">
              {n} / {label}
            </p>
            <h2>
              {title.split("\n").map((line) => (
                <span>
                  {line}
                  <br />
                </span>
              ))}
            </h2>
            <p>{body}</p>
            {n === "04" ? (
              <button class="button secondary" data-command>
                Try quick dock <kbd>Ctrl K</kbd>
              </button>
            ) : (
              <a
                class="text-link"
                href={
                  n === "02"
                    ? "/docs/usage-limits"
                    : n === "03"
                      ? "/docs/switch-profiles"
                      : "/docs/add-profile"
                }
              >
                Read the details ↗
              </a>
            )}
          </section>
        ))}
      </div>
      <figure class="sequence-media" data-focus="01">
        <div class="media-label mono">ACTUAL INTERFACE / SAMPLE DATA</div>
        <div class="screen-crop">
          <img
            src="/media/veydock-codex-switcher-windows.webp"
            width="1600"
            height="1000"
            loading="lazy"
            alt="Development VeyDock interface showing independent account usage meters"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption id="scene-caption">
          Configured profiles, without a fixed limit.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="trust wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL CONTROL / OPEN SOURCE</p>
    <div class="trust-title">
      <h2>
        A utility you can
        <br />
        <span>look inside.</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        MIT licensed. Created by Mithil Katkoria.
        <br />
        An independent project, built in the open.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="trust-rows">
      <a href="/security">
        <strong>Authentication stays with Codex.</strong>
        <span>Normal OpenAI sign-in. No ChatGPT password form.</span>
        <b>↗</b>
      </a>
      <a href="/security#local-data">
        <strong>Local does not mean risk-free.</strong>
        <span>Saved authentication and backups are sensitive files.</span>
        <b>↗</b>
      </a>
      <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/VERIFICATION.md`}>
        <strong>Evidence before promises.</strong>
        <span>Read what was tested, and what still needs verification.</span>
        <b>↗</b>
      </a>
      <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>
        <strong>MIT. Yours to inspect and adapt.</strong>
        <span>
          Keep the copyright and licence notice. Respect the branding.
        </span>
        <b>↗</b>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="final-download wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">READY TO DOCK?</p>
    <div>
      <h2>
        A clearer view.
        <br />A deliberate next move.
      </h2>
      <a class="button" href="/download">
        Get VeyDock for Windows <span>↓</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mono">v{r.version} / WINDOWS X64 / UNSIGNED PRERELEASE</p>
    <p class="alpha-note">
      The public build is alpha software. Windows may show an unknown-publisher
      warning. Account-switch acceptance and installer-driven updating are not
      yet fully verified.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
